// Problem Statement

Given an integer num, repeatedly add all its digits until the result has only one digit, and return it.

Approach: Repeated Digit Sum

Run a loop while num >= 10, because we need to continue until only one digit remains.

Initialize sum = 0.

Extract each digit using num % 10 and add it to sum.

Remove the last digit using num /= 10.

Assign sum back to num and repeat.

Return num when it becomes a single digit.//









class Solution {
    public int addDigits(int num) {
        while (num >= 10) {
            int sum = 0;

            while (num > 0) {
                sum += num % 10;
                num /= 10;
            }

            num = sum;
        }

        return num;
    }
}
